  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Health International Financing (Pandemic Fund - FIF)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Global Health (GH)):  The World Bank Financial Intermediary Fund (FIF) for Pandemic Prevention, Preparedness, and Response provides a dedicated stream of long-term financing to strengthen critical pandemic prevention, preparedness, and response (PPR) capabilities in low- and middle-income countries through investments and technical support at the national, regional, and global levels. USAID closely coordinates with FIF implementing entities and recipient countries to amplify and leverage FIF investments in pandemic prevention, preparedness, and response. These efforts strengthen health security capacities in partner countries as reflected, in part, by improved scores on various World Health Organization (WHO) health security monitoring instruments.  $2,700,000 of FY24 funds will be provided to the Central America countries of Honduras and Belize for these activities.</narrative>
  </description>
